/Title (The Convention on the Rights of the Child \(CRC\) is one of the most widely ratified international human rights treaties in history. It recognises that every child has the right to healthcare, nutrition, education, protection, and development. The treaty encouraged governments to improve child welfare systems and expand access to healthcare services, especially for vulnerable children.)
