/Title (The United Kingdom has traditionally been a major supporter of global health and development initiatives through Official Development Assistance \(ODA\). The UK has contributed significantly to organisations such as GAVI, UNICEF, and WHO, supporting immunisation campaigns, maternal healthcare, and nutrition programs in low-income countries. However, recent reductions in foreign aid budgets have raised concerns about the future of several healthcare and child welfare programs.)
